    <string name="console_eyebrow">Lanyard / Lab</string>
    <string name="console_title">Payload Runner</string>
    <string name="console_subtitle">Stages the Open Crown page-cache relays on an exact verified target. One boot, reboot clears, never automatic.</string>
    <string name="console_warning_title">Quarantined research payload</string>
    <string name="console_warning_body">This writes a kernel page-cache patch into a root-executed library. The init relay never returns to init, so the next init log can consume the logging thread and the phone may watchdog-reset. It is memory-only and disappears at reboot. Run it only on the verified lab device, and only with a recovery path.</string>

